#41100
Credits Room for Locker area~
This area was originally created by Imhotep at an unknown date.  Because of
locker shortages, more rooms and lockers have been added.  Currently this area
is using zone 411 for the rooms and mobiles.  Objects (the lockers) use zones
411, 412, and 413.

Find out how to add more lockers by using <&08Look addlocker&00>.

Zone Edit by Xiuhtecuhtli 09/23/07
~
411 576 4 0 0 0 255 0
E
addlocker~
&11Adding Lockers&00
Check available objects that the VNUM_ZONE is set to in lockers.c (currently
using zone 413). Use zedit to load the locker object into a room in zone 411.    

&11Creating New Locker Zones&00
Use the tmplocker file as a template (sys/world/obj). Make sure you change 
VNUMS after using the template to the current zone VNUMS you plan to use. Also 
the capacity weight MUST be set to 0 on the locker object. In the src directory 
select lib/specials/lockers.c and edit the VNUM_START, VNUM_MAX, and VNUM_ZONE.
~
S
#41101
Entrance to the Samsera Vaults~
You have entered a large room surrounded by walls several feet thick of
chiseled stone.  A set of stairs made out of wooden planks leads to a room
above.  There is also a set of stone steps that leads deep into the catacombs
of the Samsera vaults.  A &09sign&00 hangs on the wall, perhaps you should read
it.    
~
411 8 0 0 0 0 255 0
D0
~
~
0 0 41301
D2
~
vault~
1 0 18086
D4
~
~
0 0 41199
D5
~
~
0 0 41198
E
sign~
&10Samsera Self Storage Policy&00

Access to lockers is provided as a service to citizens of Samsera.
However, the bank cannot take responsibility for security.  If you
purchase a locker, you are ultimately responsible for making sure you
keep it closed, and any items that get lost through thievery, accident
or otherwise, are unfortunately lost.

Each locker is protected by a magical field.  If you wish to allow
another access to your locker, you must ask a God to grant your
request.  You may only have access to one locker, so if you are
granted access to another's locker, you will not be able to purchase a
locker of your own.

The Bank has done everything it can to provide a secure and reliable
self storage facility, and hopes that its patrons continue to enjoy
its services.

Yours,
  The Manager, Samsera Banking
~
S
